Windows always resolves its own host name (and "", which ws2_32 maps to
it).  OpenBSD has no nss-myhostname, so getaddrinfo() fails for the host
name unless it is in /etc/hosts.  On EAI_NONAME for the local host name,
answer with the addresses of the up, non-loopback interfaces (no IPv6
link-local), resolved numerically with the caller's hints and service, or
with localhost if there are none.  ws2_32 protocol test: 19 -> 1 failures.

